          {
            "adopted_sha256": "0426ace03159c5f29d61186a74f6592d38a60db8072ed9dafdfb80ba63bfb180",
            "audio_path": "er110_output/family_y_redelivery_audio_01/audio/r0/b1b/narration/full_story_part3.wav",
            "canonical_text": "It just doesn't sit right with me to pay for redelivery. My husband and I are both out of the house for work, so for packages where I can choose, I pick a day and time when I know I'll be home. But once, I chose a morning time slot and the package didn't come. I went out to take care of an errand, and when I got back, there was a delivery notice. Many packages don't let you choose a delivery time, either, so you don't know ahead of time when they'll arrive. Before charging us, I want them to first do something about showing up at the time we chose and telling us when the package will arrive. The delivery workers are probably having a hard time because they're short-staffed, and maybe it can't be helped. But I can't accept having to pay for that. Am I wrong to feel that way?",
